# 📚 BookVerse – Discover Your Next Favourite Read

**A personalized book recommendation platform powered by Machine Learning.**

BookVerse aims to make discovering your next favourite book easier. Instead of endlessly scrolling through book lists, users can rate books they've already read, explore new titles, and receive personalized recommendations based on their reading preferences.

The idea is simple: **Tell us what you love reading, and let the recommendation engine do the magic!** ✨

---

## 🎯 Project Objectives

The goal is to build a personalized book recommendation system that:

- Allows users to explore and rate books.
- Recommends books based on individual reading preferences.
- Identifies similarities between books using machine learning.
- Discovers hidden reading patterns from user ratings.
- Provides an interactive platform for book lovers.

## 📊 Dataset

We plan to use the [Goodbooks-10k Dataset](https://github.com/zygmuntz/goodbooks-10k).

The dataset contains approximately:
- 10,000 books.
- 6 million ratings.
- 53,000 users.
- Book metadata, tags, and reading preferences.

### Dataset Structure

```text
GoodBooks-10k/
│
├── books.csv          # Book information and metadata
├── ratings.csv        # User-book ratings
├── book_tags.csv      # Tags associated with books
├── tags.csv           # Tag names and identifiers
└── to_read.csv        # Books users want to read
```

## 🛠️ Data Preprocessing

Before training the recommendation models, the dataset will undergo cleaning and preprocessing.

Planned operations:

- Handling missing values.
- Removing duplicate books and ratings.
- Validating book IDs across datasets.
- Handling missing book image URLs.
- Preparing user-item interaction matrices.
- Processing book titles, authors, and tags.
- Filtering users and books with insufficient ratings where necessary.

## 🧠 Recommendation Engine

The project will explore multiple recommendation approaches.

### 1. Collaborative Filtering

Recommends books based on user preferences and rating patterns.

The system identifies users with similar reading interests and recommends books that similar users enjoyed.

### 2. Matrix Factorization (FunkSVD)

Uses latent user and book representations to discover hidden relationships in rating data.

The model learns embeddings for users and books and predicts how a user might rate an unseen book.

### 3. Content-Based Filtering

Recommends books based on their attributes, such as:

- Book titles
- Authors
- Genres
- Tags

Techniques such as TF-IDF and cosine similarity will help identify books with similar characteristics.

### 4. Hybrid Recommendation System

The long-term goal is to combine collaborative and content-based filtering to create a hybrid recommendation engine that provides more relevant and diverse recommendations.

## 🚀 Planned Features

- [ ] User registration and authentication.
- [ ] Browse and search books.
- [ ] Rate and review books.
- [ ] Personalized book recommendations.
- [ ] Similar-book discovery.
- [ ] Genre-based recommendations.
